---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const interpretBoundariesResult = await interpretBoundaries(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const mapMeasurementsResult = await mapMeasurements(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, interpretBoundariesResult.accepted);
const reconcileAttributionResult = await reconcileAttribution(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, mapMeasurementsResult.accepted);
const substantiateClaimsResult = await substantiateClaims(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, reconcileAttributionResult.accepted);
const assembleSubmissionResult = await assembleSubmission(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, substantiateClaimsResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { interpretBoundaries: interpretBoundariesResult, mapMeasurements: mapMeasurementsResult, reconcileAttribution: reconcileAttributionResult, substantiateClaims: substantiateClaimsResult, assembleSubmission: assembleSubmissionResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...interpretBoundariesResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...mapMeasurementsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...reconcileAttributionResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...substantiateClaimsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...assembleSubmissionResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...interpretBoundariesResult.checks, ...mapMeasurementsResult.checks, ...reconcileAttributionResult.checks, ...substantiateClaimsResult.checks, ...assembleSubmissionResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — A contractor reports an activity already in internal records: deduplicate the physical event before aggregation. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (deduplicate the physical event before aggregation.) through the existing stage result for ReportingBoundary; preserve exact source/version and the prior ReportingBoundary, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — A meter is replaced mid-period: preserve calibration and continuity assumptions. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (preserve calibration and continuity assumptions.) through the existing stage result for ReportingBoundary; preserve exact source/version and the prior ReportingBoundary, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — An estimate becomes a measurement later: version and restate affected results explicitly. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (version and restate affected results explicitly.) through the existing stage result for ReportingBoundary; preserve exact source/version and the prior ReportingBoundary, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — Organizational scope changes: separate boundary effects from operational improvement. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (separate boundary effects from operational improvement.) through the existing stage result for ReportingBoundary; preserve exact source/version and the prior ReportingBoundary, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — A public claim exceeds the report’s evidence: block publication until qualified or substantiated. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (block publication until qualified or substantiated.) through the existing stage result for ReportingBoundary; preserve exact source/version and the prior ReportingBoundary, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, interpretBoundaries: interpretBoundariesResult, mapMeasurements: mapMeasurementsResult, reconcileAttribution: reconcileAttributionResult, substantiateClaims: substantiateClaimsResult, assembleSubmission: assembleSubmissionResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
